### Cryptographic Release Verification Flow

APT verifies repository integrity using asymmetric cryptography:

1. APT fetches the uncompressed inline-signed metadata file `InRelease` (or `Release` paired with `Release.gpg`).
2. The GPG signature on `InRelease` is validated using trusted public keys stored in `/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/kali-archive-keyring.gpg`.
3. Upon validating the signature, APT parses `InRelease`, which contains cryptographically secure hashes (SHA-256) of all package indexes (`Packages.xz`, `Sources.xz`).
4. APT downloads `Packages.xz`, verifies its SHA-256 hash against `InRelease`, uncompresses it, and reads the package-specific hashes.
5. Downloaded `.deb` archives are hashed prior to `dpkg` execution to confirm authenticity and detect payload tampering.

